cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use, adapt, or reference this work, please cite it as
  shown below.
type: dataset
title: >-
  SWE Assistant: A Curated Collection of Claude AI Skills for
  Software Engineers
authors:
  - family-names: Merrien
    given-names: Tanguy
    email: tmerrien@outlook.com
abstract: >-
  A curated collection of Claude AI skills for software engineers,
  organized by recurring engineering situations and informed by
  established engineering literature. Each skill is a Markdown
  document with YAML frontmatter (Anthropic skills format) that
  surfaces coaching prompts — checklists, frames, and questions —
  drawn from sources such as The Missing Readme (Riccomini &
  Ryaboy), Working Effectively with Legacy Code (Feathers),
  A Philosophy of Software Design (Ousterhout), Designing
  Data-Intensive Applications (Kleppmann), and the Agile
  Manifesto. The skills are designed to
  prompt practitioner thinking rather than replace it, supporting
  the climb through Broadwell's stages of competence in early- and
  mid-career software engineering. Intended for students, junior
  engineers, educators, and curriculum designers.
keywords:
  - software-engineering
  - engineering-education
  - junior-engineer
  - claude-ai
  - claude-skills
  - coaching
  - pedagogy
  - open-educational-resources
  - mentoring
  - professional-development
